endearing, navy background. Bold comic ink shadows, enamel white and steel blue, no cream, no text, no humans, no trademarks.`\n  - **Parameters:** `backend`: `\"Gemini 3.1 Flash Lite Image\"`, `aspect_ratio`: `\"1:1 (1K)\"`, `seed`: `42`\n- **`SHELF_CONTROL_Prompt` (`16e3a70a`)** $\\rightarrow$ **`e4b407bf` (`fast_text_to_image`)**:\n  - **Prompt:** `512px square original painted comic game portrait of SHELF CONTROL, angry red pixel face on a navy checkout-monitor robot with a receipt paper crown, navy background. Bold comic ink shadows, enamel white and steel blue, no cream, no text, no humans, no trademarks.`\n  - **Parameters:** `backend`: `\"Gemini 3.1 Flash Lite Image\"`, `aspect_ratio`: `\"1:1 (1K)\"`, `seed`: `42`\n\n---\n\n### 3. Download Contract & Supported Retrieval Mechanisms\n\n#### Web Editor Interface\n1. **Queued ZIP Archive:**\n   - A packaged archive named `hungry_for_trouble_assets.zip` (Download ID: `8005f076-7e6c-46b3-929f-85c4c0f7f150`) has been queued containing all three assets (`audio/hungry_for_trouble_theme.mp3`, `portraits/mop3_portrait.png`, and `portraits/shelf_control_portrait.png`).\n   - The download card appears above the chat input in the editor. If not immediately visible, reloading the page restores all saved download cards.\n2. **Direct Node Output Download:**\n   - In the canvas, each node's output card and header ellipsis menu provide a direct single-asset download action for collaborators.\n\n#### External MCP Client / Automated Retrieval Contract (Without Sharing or API Export)\n- Direct public unauthenticated download URLs are deliberately unavailable for private projects to prevent unauthorized exposure.\n- **Supported Retrieval Flow:**\n  1. Grant workspace access to the project by calling `set_project_team_access(team_access=\"workspace_read\")` (or `\"workspace_edit\"`). This permanently publishes the generated project files to the shared workspace Asset Catalog without public sharing or API export.\n  2. Call `get_workspace_asset(fid=\"<FILE_UUID>\")` with the asset's file ID.\n  3. The response provides compact metadata and an authenticated Atlas download URL.\n  4. Fetch the download URL using an HTTP `GET` request with the workspace Bearer token header:\n     ```http\n     GET <download_url>\n     Authorization: Bearer <WORKSPACE_API_KEY>\n     ```",
